{"slug": "c12-frontier-xu-sang-structured-moment", "round": 12, "kind": "deepen", "verdict": "precise-obstruction", "claim": "Part B only; nothing about zeros of zeta; no R4 answer. Xu-Sang 2610.17675 v2 Theorem 1.2 (prime second moment, Q^((37-10 sqrt6)/6) = Q^2.084184, rows and primes of the same length) was read in the manuscript text and compared line by line with slots M1, M2 of Liu II (13.2), (13.3) and the Z11 count. Outcome (iii): it fits neither. M1/M2 are closed by the range (theorem at prime length z = 1; M1 needs z < 1/2, M2 z < 3/13, probe supply 0.21) and the shape (no witness factor). As a Chebyshev count option for Z11 it is never selected: exact identity N - delta - R0(delta) = 6(delta - delta*)^2/(15 - 6 delta) >= 0 (the moment is dominated by the x = 0 count it was derived from), and R(delta, x) <= R(delta, 0); 0 of 34680 exact classes; at the critical class 0.614839 against 0.590332 (needs below Q^2.059677). Abscissa unchanged: 0.8748866470 (30 digits 0.874886647039964130944614000530). Frontier slot withdrawn from round 13.", "refereeHolds": null, "referees": 0, "r1": false, "r2": false, "r3": false, "r4": false, "aboutZeros": false, "file": "tmp/research-2026-11-16/push/c12-frontier-xu-sang-structured-moment/RESULT.md", "nodes": [], "tags": ["frontier", "part-B", "Xu-Sang-2610.17675", "structured-prime-moment", "Z11", "M1", "M2", "slot-withdrawn"], "obstructionKind": "moment derived from a count by bins returns at most that count under Chebyshev; prime length outside slot capacity", "restatement": false, "knownArchitecture": true, "brokenProved": 0, "lemmasDecided": 2, "partB": {"figure": 0.874886647, "changed": false, "dependsOn": ["openai/math 7/8 manuscript (30 Sep 2026)", "Liu 2610.12234", "Liu 2610.26835 v2", "Xu-Sang 2610.15291"], "newInputEntersDependencyList": false}, "score": 0, "heavy": false, "lesson": "A structured moment proved as sup over bins of count x size^2 cannot improve the count it came from; an input can move the count only