{"slug": "c12-bost-connes-crossed-product-duality", "round": 12, "kind": "explore", "verdict": "OBSTRUCTION: device closed at stage A; E_a passes every marked step in its tensor system and T-NR (c > 2) is a positive density in the Bost-Connes algebra itself", "claim": "Nothing about zeros of zeta. Positivity in A = C*(Q/Z) x N^x: (C) every sigma-invariant state factors through C(Z^); KMS_beta is a product measure for every beta > 0 and its values on the algebraic Hecke algebra are entire in beta from finitely many primes, zeta-free. (V) Archimedean vector states sum f(lambda k) e_k: Mellin of each matrix coefficient = periodic zeta times an archimedean factor; read set {L(s,chi)}; the mu_n step and the Poisson step are identities, the inequality is a square. (B) Bochner positivity on lines sigma > 1 only; false on 0 < sigma < 1 since zeta(sigma) < 0. (W) Weil prime side = phi_{1/2}(H_g), H_g = sum Lambda(n) g(log n) mu_n mu_n^*. (T) T-NR with c > 2 = phi_beta(D .), D = 1 + c sqrt(q) P_q + q P_{q^2} >= 1 in A: inner perturbation of the dynamics; differs only in exact mu_q covariance at one prime. DH fails at the sign of its density, not at the mu_n step. Closure covers three classes of states, not all states. Author referee pass only.", "refereeHolds": true, "referees": 1, "refereeNote": "author adversarial pass, not independent; three wording corrections applied", "r1": false, "r2": false, "r3": false, "r4": false, "aboutZeros": false, "file": "tmp/research-2026-11-16/push/c12-bost-connes-crossed-product-duality/RESULT.md", "nodes": [], "tags": ["bost-connes", "crossed-product", "KMS", "poisson-summation", "hecke-algebra", "CROSS-1", "RS-1", "T-NR", "E_a", "weil-form", "stage-A"], "obstructionKind": "positivity of a state is a square that holds for a control; duality steps are identities; Bochner positivity lost at the pole", "restatement": false, "knownArchitecture": false, "brokenProved": 0, "lemmasDecided": 1}
{"round": 12, "slug": "c12-repair-sources-statement-o-v3", "kind": "repair", "verdict": "partial-result", "claim": "Record lane; no attack; nothing about zeros of zeta. Five primary sources opened. Bohr 1916 Satz A and Kaczorowski-Perelli 1999 Theorems 2, 3 match the statements used; Hamburger 1921 matches with one hypothesis tighter (f absolutely convergent for sigma > 1). Huxley 1972 states the gap bound and the density estimate with exponent 12/5, not a count of primes in short intervals: DEL is relabelled 'relative to S(theta)' (deduction per Ingham 1937, not opened). Bettin 2016 gives exact reciprocity at s = 1/2 with integer shifts (primes in moment form, coprime integers in Estermann form), none for abs(L(1/2+it,chi))^2 with t != 0. Second referee on the control tables of the three round-11 stage-A closures: all hold, no PROVED step broken, seven corrections (T-NR lift zero in the strip only for c < p0^(1/2)+p0^(-1/2); E_a lift has a degree-two functional equation; E_a is not a pass of the twist-modulus candidate). Statement O version 3 reader pass written; device count 11 / 23. Map 182 -> 186 rows (P53, G32, Q28, Z34). Engine: three device types closed; 1,659 nodes, 8,922 edges, 36,558 generated, 8,437 scored.", "aboutZeros": false, "refHolds": false, "threeReferees": false, "allHold": false, "r1": false, "r2": false, "r3": false, "r4": false, "score": 0, "errors": "No independent referee yet. REFEREE.md is the author's own check (reservations R-1 to R-7). REFEREE2.md is this lane's second-referee report on c11-rs1-regular-rep-matrix-bridge, c11-rs1-twist-modulus-reciprocity, c11-rs3-debranges-positivity-family (all hold; corrections R-1 to R-3, T-1 to T-3, B-1). Own error corrected: a map row first placed as S13, moved to Q28.", "surviving": "Three stage-A closures with two referee files each on the control tables; source table with five opened texts; DEL relative to a counting statement whose density input is opened; Statement O version 3 (reader pass) as the current text via map row O1; map rows P53, G32, Q28, Z34; three device types closed in the engine.", "lesson": "A citation read at second hand can name the right paper and the wrong statement: the 1972 paper gives a density estimate and a gap bound, and the short-interval count used by the control is a separate deduction; and a control table entry such as 'functional equation: yes' needs the degree and root number written next to it, since the two passing lifts keep different halves of the target's structure.", "followUp": "Open Ingham 1937 (or a textbook proof) for the short-interval count; independent referee for c11-del-device-read-confirm; owner decision on the two euler waiters, which wait on each other and compute nothing.", "file": "tmp/research-2026-11-16/push/c12-repair-sources-statement-o-v3/RESULT.md", "heavy": false, "refereeHolds": null, "referees": 0, "restatement": false, "knownArchitecture": false, "brokenProved": 0, "lemmasDecided": 0, "obstructionKind": "record: sources opened, control tables confirmed, labels corrected", "nodes": [], "tags": ["record", "referee", "primary-sources", "statement-o", "control", "map", "engine"]}
